<p>
I went to <a href="https://www.tcan.ca/events-list/an-evening-with-valrie-plante">An Evening with Valérie Plante</a> to learn about her experience
in prioritizing the environment during her two terms as the mayor of
Montréal. It was interesting to hear about the <a href="https://montreal.ca/en/articles/infrastructures-and-developments-designed-to-capture-and-absorb-heavy-rainfall-68389">sponge parks</a> that they
built in order to absorb excess rainwater, designing <a href="https://montreal.ca/en/topics/pedestrian-streets">pedestrian streets</a> for beauty and comfort, the importance of connecting with
public transit, and how they built an <a href="https://montreal.ca/en/articles/ebn-montreals-express-bike-network-4666">express bike network</a> as
part of improving safety for everyone, including the data they
collected in order to make the case.
</p>

<p>
Her key tips were:
</p>

<ol class="org-ol">
<li>Build partnerships</li>
<li>Support citizens' initiatives</li>
<li>Connect with what people care about</li>
</ol>

